{"a":"DDInter1683","b":"DDInter513","level":"Minor","mech":["Absorption"],"description":"Antacids and agents with acid-neutralizing effects may impair the absorption of dexamethasone, prednisolone, prednisone, and other corticosteroids, although data from published studies are somewhat conflicting. The mechanism of interaction and clinical significance are unknown. No particular intervention is necessary during concomitant therapy with these agents, but clinicians should be aware of the potential for interaction. abdominal pain Acidosis acute pancreatitis adrenal insufficiency agranulocytoses anaemia angina ascites aspergillosis atelectasis More","management":"-","iid":986786},
