{"a":"DDInter1683","b":"DDInter638","level":"Minor","mech":["Absorption"],"description":"Coadministration with antacids may decrease the oral bioavailability of captopril and other angiotensin converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors due to delayed gastric emptying and/or elevated gastric pH. Based on available data, the clinical significance of this interaction appears to be minor. As a precaution, patients may want to consider separating the administration times of ACE inhibitors and antacids or oral medications that contain antacids (e.g., didanosine buffered tablets or pediatric oral solution) by 1 to 2 hours. agranulocytoses anaemia Anorexia aspergillosis Bacterial infection bacterial pneumonia chest pain allergic dermatitis contact dermatitis diabetic acidosis More","management":"-","iid":1046108},
