{"a":"DDInter1683","b":"DDInter826","level":"Moderate","mech":["Absorption"],"description":"INTERVAL: Some antacids have been reported to increase the rate of absorption and, rarely, the extent of absorption of oral sulfonylureas. The hypoglycemic effects of these agents may be altered. anaemia angina Anorexia constipated dehydration Diabetes diarrhea dyspepsia Difficulty breathing gall bladder More","management":"Sulfonylureas should be administered at least two hours before or after antacids when possible. Regular monitoring of blood sugar is advisable. In addition, patients should be apprised of the signs and symptoms of hypoglycemia (e.g., headache, dizziness, drowsiness, nausea, hunger, tremor, weakness, sweating, palpitations), how to treat it, and to contact their physician if it occurs.","iid":1053052},
