{"a":"DDInter48","b":"DDInter883","level":"Moderate","mech":["Excretion"],"description":"Serious hypersensitivity reactions to allopurinol have been well-documented in the medical literature. Case reports have suggested that thiazide diuretics may increase the risk of allopurinol-induced hypersensitivity reactions, especially in patients with renal insufficiency. Alcoholic intoxication alopecia allergic alveolitis Amnesia animal bite anosmia Anxiety Aphonia Aching joints arthritis More","management":"Patients should be advised to promptly report any signs of hypersensitivity, including rash, pruritus, fever, or chills.","iid":964288},
